why why can't fall asleep avoid  electronics before bed blue light from a  screen simulates daylight and causes  your brain to produce cortisol a stress  hormone that wakes you up do not nap  during the day with every waking hour  your body's desire to sleep increases  not being resets your sleep drive and  can keep you awake at night have a  regular sleep schedule even on weekends  your body has a natural biological clock  called the circadian rhythm sleeping in  or staying up late can disrupt this  rhythm and make it harder to fall asleep  the next night don't drink alcohol  before bed as alcohol leaves your system  it disrupts your restful REM sleep and  can even cause nightmares use your bed  only for two things sleep and sex using  Pavlovian conditioning you can  strengthen your body's association  between bed and sleep remove work TV and  phones from your bedroom bed equals  sleep also  when orgasm releases oxytocin and  vasopressin two hormones that lower  stress levels and improve relaxation  keep your body temperature cool your  body's temperature naturally decreases  during sleep you can help it out by  lowering your thermostat and not  exercising before bed  sweet dreams
 

